{"base":"96251f128e2d0f5f58f05d5064672b37474ef409","description":"Merge share crate into main crate\n\nThe share crate duplicated iroh endpoint config, CID utilities,\nkey conversion, and directory walk logic that other consumers\nalso needed. Consolidate into the main crate behind a feature\nflag so consumers share one implementation and rad-artifact\ngets fetch/serve commands out of the box.\n\n- Add `share` feature flag (default-enabled) with iroh,\n  blake3, tokio, ureq, walkdir, dunce as optional deps\n- Move share/src/lib.rs into src/share/ as 5 modules:\n  endpoint, cid, keys, fetch, serve\n- Absorb cid/fetch/serve CLI commands into rad-artifact\n- Make cid_to_blake3_hash and CID constants public\n- Add canonical_walk and compute_content_id with golden\n  hash and determinism tests\n- Add did_to_iroh_public_key and radicle_secret_to_iroh\n  key conversion utilities\n- Update add_collection to use canonical_walk for\n  robust cross-platform directory traversal\n- Document sync/async design tradeoffs on fetch functions\n- Delete standalone share workspace member\n\n\nPrint confirmation on mutating commands\n\n- Add stderr messages for locate, attest, remove-location\n- Improve add output to describe what was done\n- Follows CLI guideline: \"if you change state, tell the user\"\n\n\nAdd --no-input flag and TTY check\n\n- Add global --no-input flag to disable interactive prompts\n- Check stdin is a TTY before entering interactive picker\n- Scripts/CI won't hang waiting for input anymore\n- Error message tells user what args to pass instead\n\n\nAdd examples to subcommand help text\n\n- Add after_long_help examples for all subcommands\n- Examples show with --help but not with -h (concise)\n- Cover common workflows: cid+add, locate, show, list, fetch, serve\n\n\nAuto-detect TTY for output format\n\n- Pretty output by default in terminals, JSON when piped\n- Add --json flag to force JSON in a terminal\n- Keep --pretty flag for forcing human-readable in pipes\n- Update top-level description to reflect new behavior\n\n\nSuggest next commands after mutations\n\n- After add, suggest locate to add a download location\n- After locate, suggest show --pretty to verify\n- Only show hints when stderr is a terminal\n\n\nColor ERROR prefix red in terminal\n\n- Bold red ERROR when stderr is a TTY\n- Respects NO_COLOR environment variable\n- Falls back to plain text when piped or NO_COLOR is set\n\n\nChange redact reason to --reason/-m flag\n\n- Reason was a positional arg, awkward for free-form strings\n- Now uses -m/--reason like git commit's -m flag\n- Add examples to redact help text\n\n\nEnforce fetch both-or-neither at parse time\n\n- Use clap requires to enforce OID and CID are both-or-neither\n- Constraint now visible in help text\n- Remove manual validation, replace with unreachable\n\n\nStream iroh downloads to disk with progress\n\n- Replace in-memory buffering with FsStore-backed downloads\n- Add indicatif progress bar (spinner + bytes + speed)\n- Uniform FsStore approach for both blobs and collections\n- Shared fetch_iroh_to_store core with mpsc progress channel\n- HTTP downloads stream to temp file, verify CID from disk\n- download() now takes &Path instead of &mut dyn Write\n- Add verify_cid_file for streaming hash verification\n- Guaranteed cleanup: db.shutdown() before temp dir drop\n\n\nDrop tempfile runtime dep, use manual dirs\n\n- Use .rad-artifact-fetch-{hash} dir like sendme\n- Use .partial file for HTTP downloads\n- tempfile stays as dev-dep only for tests\n- Clean up store dir and partial files on error\n\n\ncli: prefer flags in place of positional args\n\n- CID is now --cid flag on all subcommands\n- Name is now --name/-n flag on add\n- Merge locate/remove-location into location add/remove\n- OID stays positional (it's the primary noun)\n- URL stays positional on location add/remove\n- Update all examples in help text\n\n\ncli: accept shorthand commits via revparse\n\n- Rename <OID> positional arg to <COMMIT> across all subcommands\n- Accept abbreviated hashes and tag names, not just full 40-char OIDs\n- Resolve user input through git revparse_single before lookup\n- Add error::Resolve for clear messages on invalid refs\n- Fix misleading Fetch help text (\"Git object ID of the release\")\n- Fix broken Add example that showed v1.0.0 (rejected by Oid parser)\n\n\nScope release lookups to delegates\n\nWithout this, a non-delegate could create a release for a commit\nand block delegates from creating one (squatting). Scoping to\ndelegates also lets every command accept a commit OID instead of\nrequiring users to know the internal release COB ID.\n\n- Filter find_by_oid to only delegate-authored releases\n- Prevent non-delegate releases from shadowing delegate ones\n- Replace library find_or_create_by_oid with local version\n- Fetch delegates once in run() and thread to all handlers\n- Add tests for delegate filtering and ambiguity detection\n- Update README CLI usage and document delegate scoping","oid":"02e5bf2737533da3790a2485f82dc845f4a3d34b","type":"revision"}